From a93924dfd0c90354a663adcf546b3fe4e8389416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agentic_apr <xianng.24@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:51:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch build: reconfigure if the build dir is missing

The rebuild path (inplace_rebuild) skipped cmake and ran 'ninja -C build_<sha>', so a
build dir lost to a prior sanitizer rebuild's 'git clean -dfx' (or disk cleanup, or
never built) made a CORRECT patch fail instantly with 'ninja: fatal: chdir - No such
file or directory'. Now cmake reconfigures on a rebuild when build.ninja is absent; a
warm build dir still rebuilds incrementally.

Verified: cppcheck 192c30ab (build_<sha> wiped) reconfigures, builds, and the correct
tokAt(5) fix passes (rc=0), instead of a 0s chdir fast-fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../projects_v1/common_build_tpl.jinja        | 53 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/defectsc_tpl/projects_v1/common_build_tpl.jinja b/defectsc_tpl/projects_v1/common_build_tpl.jinja
index a566cc4..b919132 100644
--- a/defectsc_tpl/projects_v1/common_build_tpl.jinja
+++ b/defectsc_tpl/projects_v1/common_build_tpl.jinja
@@ -1,19 +1,42 @@
 build_dir=$1
 test_log=$2
 
-
-
-
-{%if not is_rebuild %}
-	cmake_flags="{{build_flags|join(" ") }}"
-	
-	cmake \
-	$cmake_flags \
-	-G Ninja -B $build_dir 
-
-
-{%endif%}
-
-
-ninja -C $build_dir 
+cmake_flags="{{build_flags|join(" ") }}"
+
+# Configure on a fresh build; on a rebuild (patch test), re-configure ONLY if the
+# build dir was lost — cleaned by a prior sanitizer rebuild's `git clean -dfx`, by
+# disk cleanup, or never built. Otherwise `ninja -C $build_dir` dies with
+# "chdir ... No such file or directory" and a CORRECT patch is falsely marked failed.
+{% if is_rebuild %}
+if [ ! -f "$build_dir/build.ninja" ]; then
+	echo "build dir missing — reconfiguring before rebuild"
+	cmake $cmake_flags -G Ninja -B $build_dir
+fi
+{% else %}
+cmake $cmake_flags -G Ninja -B $build_dir
+{% endif %}
+
+
+{% if scope_test %}
+# Scoped build (sanitizer path): build ONLY the failing test's executable, not the
+# whole project — an ASan build of an entire project is huge and times out. Resolve
+# the ctest test name (test_flags) to its executable target via ctest's JSON, then
+# ninja just that. Falls back to a full build if resolution fails.
+_tgt=$(ctest --test-dir $build_dir --show-only=json-v1 -R "{{ test_flags|join('|') }}" 2>/dev/null | python3 -c '
+import json,sys,os
+try:
+    d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(os.path.relpath(d["tests"][0]["command"][0], sys.argv[1]))
+except Exception:
+    pass
+' "$build_dir")
+if [ -n "$_tgt" ]; then
+	echo "scoped sanitizer build target: $_tgt"
+	ninja -C $build_dir -j {{cpu_count}} "$_tgt"
+else
+	echo "scope_test: could not resolve target, building all"
+	ninja -C $build_dir -j {{cpu_count}}
+fi
+{% else %}
+ninja -C $build_dir -j {{cpu_count}}
+{% endif %}
 
-- 
